## Scope
Skills are on-demand expertise. `name` must match the folder that contains `SKILL.md`.

## Three kinds
- **Tech** (`<topic>-v<major>/`, e.g. `fastify-v5`): committed in this repo. Agent-invocable. Required sections: Scope, Assumptions, Principles, Constraints, Interactions
- **Patterns** (unversioned, e.g. `composition-patterns`, `frontend-design`): committed. Agent-invocable craft and guidelines
- **Workflow** (`.agents/skills/w-<name>/`): slash-only, installed from basilic-skills. Set `disable-model-invocation: true`. One-line `description`.

## Principles
- One primary topic per skill; independent versions = separate skills
- `name` lowercase/digits/hyphens, max 64, equals folder name
- Basilic playbook names start with `w-`
- Prefer `paths` over legacy `globs` when file-scoped
- Declarative: state what is true. Patterns over long examples
- Progressive disclosure: keep `SKILL.md` short; depth in `references/` or `PATTERNS.md`
- No repo-specific paths in tech skills. Rules override skills
- Workflow descriptions stay one line (discovery tokens are always-on)

## Hierarchy
Rules (constraints) > skills (patterns) > model

Update procedure and inventory: `apps/docu/content/docs/development/cursor-skills.mdx`. Lock pins `blockmatic/basilic-skills` (`w-*`) and `mattpocock/skills`. Stack skills are committed; list: `scripts/owned-agent-skills.txt`.

Playbook bodies are numbered instructions (spec frontmatter); keep simple playbooks short. Git playbooks carry `references/git-publish.md`.
